{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"no\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"Moreover, analyses in this study focused on steps that could be reliably detected using force plate measurements and did not include episodes of hastening or true freezing.\",\n    \"Whether the observed increases in STN beta activity and intermuscular coherence during the late stance phase when OFF levodopa are associated with poor motor performance during free walking remains to be tested in future studies.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"LFPs in the STN and leg muscle activity measured as EMG of the gastrocnemius and peroneus longus were recorded in 14 PD patients during sitting, standing and stepping, ON and OFF levodopa.\",\n    \"During the stepping-in-place condition, patients were instructed to step at a comfortable and consistent frequency, and to imagine themselves walking normally.\",\n    \"This study examines the dynamics of STN and EMG activities during stepping in PD, and how they are modulated by dopaminergic medication.\",\n    \"Moreover, analyses in this study focused on steps that could be reliably detected using force plate measurements and did not include episodes of hastening or true freezing.\",\n    \"The reduction in STN beta activity appears to precede changes in EMG activity (Fig. 3A), suggesting a causal relationship where STN activity influences muscle activation.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法为no。论文确实研究了STN活动与下肢肌电活动之间的动态和时序关系，例如STN beta活动变化先于EMG活动变化，并探讨了STN beta bursts与肌肉活动的关联。但是，这些结果来自受控的原地步进任务，而非真实FOG事件。论文在Limitations中明确指出，分析没有纳入真正的冻结事件（true freezing），并明确表示相关现象与自由行走中运动障碍的关系仍有待未来研究验证。因此，不能将该研究作为真实冻结事件发生时STN活动与下肢肌肉输出时序关系的直接实验证据。指控者对研究对象、实验任务、左旋多巴比较以及未分析真实冻结事件的描述均有全文依据，判断为yes。需要区分的是：论文支持无真实冻结事件的步进任务中的STN-EMG动态关系，但不支持将该关系直接推广为真实FOG发生时的神经肌肉时序关系。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "efff4fae-3506-4f9d-a1f9-08d5a298fc5f", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": 